.TH NFTBAN 8 "April 2026" "NFTBan 1.76.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
nftban \- open-source Linux IPS and nftables firewall manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nftban
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B NFTBan
is an open-source Linux Intrusion Prevention System (IPS) and firewall manager
built on nftables. It provides kernel-native enforcement with atomic rule
updates, privilege separation via Polkit, and automated threat detection
through feeds and IDS integration.
.PP
The name
.B NFTBan
stands for
.IR "NFTables BAN actions" ,
reflecting its foundation on native nftables technology for kernel-level
packet filtering and ban enforcement.
.PP
.B Key Capabilities:
.IP "\fBAtomic Rule Updates\fR" 4
Uses native nftables transactions for rule updates without flushing
existing connections or causing network disruption.
.IP "\fBPrivilege Separation\fR" 4
Uses Polkit for granular privilege separation, enabling firewall management
without requiring full root access.
.IP "\fBThreat Detection\fR" 4
Integrates with threat intelligence feeds (Spamhaus, AbuseIPDB, Firehol) and
Suricata IDS for automated detection and response.
.IP "\fBHosting Panel Support\fR" 4
Integrates with DirectAdmin, cPanel, Plesk, CyberPanel, and other control
panels. Detects and whitelists critical service ports.
.SH ARCHITECTURE
.B NFTBan
operates through direct integration with the Linux nftables netfilter framework.
All firewall operations are executed as atomic nftables transactions. The Go
daemon (nftband) handles runtime ban/unban, IPC, and login monitoring. The Bash
CLI handles schema generation, configuration, deployment, and metrics export.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Core Commands"
.TP
.B status
Display system status including firewall state, banned IPs, and service health.
Use \fB\-\-json\fR for machine-readable output.
.TP
.B health
Run comprehensive health checks on all NFTBan components.
.TP
.B check
Verify environment and prerequisites for NFTBan operation.
.TP
.B validate
Validate configuration files for syntax and logical errors.
.TP
.B sync
Atomic reload of nftables rules preserving runtime state.
.TP
.B version
Display NFTBan version and component versions.
.TP
.B help
Show available commands and usage information.
.SS "Service Control"
.TP
.B enable \fR[\fIservice\fR]
Enable NFTBan services (all, nftables, suricata, login, timers).
.TP
.B disable \fR[\fIservice\fR]
Disable NFTBan services.
.TP
.B restart \fR[\fIservice\fR]
Restart NFTBan services.
.TP
.B services
Display status of all NFTBan-related services.
.SS "Firewall Management"
.TP
.B firewall \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Manage nftables firewall: init, reload, status, check, reset, validate, stats.
.TP
.B firewall\-logs \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Firewall log analysis: show, tail, stats, search.
.TP
.B ban \fIIP\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Ban an IP address. Options: \fB\-\-timeout\fR, \fB\-\-reason\fR, \fB\-\-permanent\fR,
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR, \fB\-\-async\fR, \fB\-\-wait\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR.
.TP
.B unban \fIIP\fR
Remove ban on an IP address.
.TP
.B protect \fR[\fIIP\fR]
Add IP to permanent protection (cannot be banned).
.TP
.B unprotect \fR[\fIIP\fR]
Remove IP from permanent protection.
.TP
.B flush \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Emergency flush/reset of nftables sets. Use with caution.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fItype\fR]
List IPs: banned, whitelist, or all. Use \fB\-\-json\fR for JSON output.
.TP
.B search \fIIP\fR
Search for an IP across all blocklists and show ban details.
.TP
.B blacklist \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Manage IP blacklist: add, remove, list, flush.
.TP
.B whitelist \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Manage IP whitelist: sync, show, whitelistme.
.TP
.B cleanup \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Manage and evict old permanent bans to free memory.
.TP
.B whitelist-system
Auto-whitelist essential system IPs (gateway, DNS, server IPs).
Ensures critical infrastructure is never blocked.
.SS "Protection Modules"
.TP
.B ddos \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
DDoS protection (L1): enable, disable, status, test.
Provides L3/L4 traffic pressure mitigation with SYN flood protection.
.TP
.B portscan \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Port scan detection: enable, disable, status, check, history, test.
.TP
.B botguard \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
HTTP bot detection (L2): enable, disable, status, config, stats.
L3/L4 live and L7 batch analysis of HTTP bot behavior.
.TP
.B botscan \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Trigger on-demand bot scan analysis.
.TP
.B login \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Login monitoring: status, enable, disable, logs, test, run.
.br
\fBenable\fR auto-installs the service and enables SSH monitoring in one step.
.br
Use \fBenable all\fR for ssh+su+sudo, or \fBenable ssh\fR for specific types.
.TP
.B suricata \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Suricata IDS integration (L3): enable, disable, status, stats, rules, alerts, config.
DPI/signature intelligence at L7. Requires Suricata package.
.TP
.B feeds \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Threat intelligence feeds: select, list, enable, disable, update, status.
.TP
.B rbl \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
RBL (Real-time Blackhole List) monitoring: check, status, providers, config.
.TP
.B trust \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Trust feeds (whitelist CDN/cloud): list, enable, disable, update, load, status.
Supports Cloudflare, AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, Fastly, and more.
.TP
.B country \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Country blocking: list, enable, disable, mode, status, apply.
Block or allow traffic by ISO country code (CN, RU, etc.).
.TP
.B tunnel \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
DNS tunnel suspicion detection: enable, disable, status, scores, history.
.TP
.B cloudflare \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Cloudflare IP management: enable, disable, update, status.
.br
\fBDEPRECATED\fR: Use \fBnftban trust enable CLOUDFLARE\fR instead for unified CDN management.
.SS "GeoIP and Geographic Blocking"
.TP
.B geoip \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
GeoIP lookups: lookup, bulk, status, test, update, config.
.TP
.B geoban \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Geographic blocking: ban, unban, whitelist, unwhitelist, list, status.
.SS "Monitoring and Reporting"
.TP
.B stats \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Statistics and monitoring. Subcommands:
.RS
.IP \fBdashboard\fR
Show statistics dashboard (default). Options: \fB\-\-json\fR, \fB\-\-last\fR, \fB\-\-since\fR, \fB\-\-until\fR.
.IP "\fBtop\fR \fItype\fR [\fIN\fR]"
Show top lists: ips, countries, jails. Example: \fBnftban stats top ips 20\fR.
.IP "\fBip\fR \fIIP\fR"
Show ban history for specific IP address.
.IP "\fBrecent\fR [\fIN\fR]"
Show recent ban activity. Use \fB\-\-follow\fR for real-time.
.IP \fBmonitor\fR
Real-time monitoring with auto-refresh. Use \fB\-\-interval\fR to set refresh rate.
.IP \fBexport\fR
Export statistics to file. Options: \fB\-\-format\fR (json/csv), \fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-\-since\fR, \fB\-\-until\fR.
.IP \fBsnapshot\fR
Create hourly statistics snapshot.
.IP \fBcleanup\fR
Cleanup old logs and snapshots. Use \fB\-\-days\fR to set retention (default: 90).
.IP \fBclear-cache\fR
Clear statistics cache.
.IP \fBcheck-alerts\fR
Check for threshold alerts.
.RE
.TP
.B watchdog \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
System resource monitoring: status, check, report, history, enable, disable.
.br
Monitors load average, memory, I/O wait, disk usage.
.br
Exports Prometheus metrics to /var/lib/nftban/metrics/watchdog.prom.
.TP
.B report \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Generate reports: generate, email, schedule, run, list.
.TP
.B metrics \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Prometheus metrics: enable, disable, status.
.TP
.B timers \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Systemd timer management: status, enable, disable.
.TP
.B mail \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Email notifications: test, send, configure.
Send reports and alerts via email.
.TP
.B benchmark \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Performance benchmarking of NFTBan components: run, results, compare.
.TP
.B scale \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Display nftables set scale levels and daemon counter status.
.TP
.B queue \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Task queue and dead-letter queue (DLQ) management: status, list, retry, flush.
.TP
.B snapshot \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Create and manage configuration and statistics snapshots: create, list, restore.
.TP
.B export \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Export data to external systems. Options: \fB\-\-format\fR (json/csv).
.TP
.B connector \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Generic connector export to external systems (Elasticsearch, Kafka, etc.): enable, disable, status.
.TP
.B zabbix \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Zabbix trapper export with multi-target support and LLD: enable, disable, status, send.
.TP
.B pro \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
NFTBan Pro subscription management and remote metrics: enroll, status, send, disable.
.SS "Configuration and Setup"
.TP
.B config \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Configuration management. Subcommands:
.RS
.IP \fBtest\fR
Validate all configuration against the JSON schema.
Reports errors, warnings, unknown keys, and deprecated keys.
Options: \fB\-\-verbose\fR (show all keys), \fB\-\-json\fR (machine-readable).
Exit codes: 0=OK, 1=warnings, 2=errors, 3=critical.
.IP \fBaudit\fR
Audit configuration for drift and changes since installation or upgrade.
Shows: overridden keys, unknown keys, deprecated keys, renamed keys, and new keys.
Options: \fB\-\-json\fR (machine-readable output).
.IP \fBshow\fR
Display effective merged configuration from all sources.
Merges base .conf files with .conf.local overrides.
Groups output by category (system, paths, features, modules).
Options: \fB\-\-json\fR (machine-readable output).
.IP \fBdiff\fR
Show differences between defaults and local overrides.
Lists all settings in .conf.local files that differ from defaults.
.IP "\fBget\fR \fIMODULE\fR"
Get configuration for specified module.
.IP "\fBset\fR \fIMODULE KEY=VALUE\fR"
Set configuration value for module.
.IP "\fBreset\fR \fIMODULE KEY\fR"
Reset configuration key to default value.
.IP "\fBdefaults\fR \fIMODULE\fR"
Show default values for module.
.IP "\fBoverrides\fR \fIMODULE\fR"
Show override values from .conf.local files.
.RE
.TP
.B configtest \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Validate configuration against schema (alias for \fBconfig test\fR).
Options: \fB\-\-verbose\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR.
.TP
.B configaudit \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Audit configuration for drift (alias for \fBconfig audit\fR).
Options: \fB\-\-json\fR.
.TP
.B setup \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Initial system setup.
.TP
.B wizard
Interactive setup wizard with step-by-step configuration.
Guides new users through initial NFTBan configuration.
.TP
.B profile \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Security profiles: select, apply, show, list.
.TP
.B permissions \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
File permissions: check, enforce, fix.
.SS "System Information"
.TP
.B module
Display installed modules inventory.
.TP
.B fhs
Check FHS (Filesystem Hierarchy Standard) compliance.
.TP
.B nftables \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Direct nftables control: start, stop, restart, reload, enable, disable, status.
.TP
.B port \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Port scanning and analysis: scan, list, summary, html-report, mail-report.
.TP
.B panel \fR[\fIpanel\fR] \fR[\fIaction\fR]
Web hosting panel firewall integration. Manages firewall ports for control panels.
.RS
.IP \fBdirectadmin\fR
DirectAdmin panel (port 2222, FTP passive 35000-35999). Includes CloudFlare whitelist.
.IP \fBcpanel\fR
cPanel/WHM (ports 2082-2087, 2095-2096, webmail).
.IP \fBcwp\fR
CentOS Web Panel (ports 2030, 2031).
.IP \fBcyberpanel\fR
CyberPanel with OpenLiteSpeed (ports 7080, 8090).
.IP \fBinterworx\fR
InterWorx panel (ports 2080, 2443).
.IP \fBvesta\fR
VestaCP/HestiaCP (port 8083).
.RE
.IP
Actions: \fBenable\fR, \fBdisable\fR, \fBstatus\fR.
.br
Example: \fBnftban panel directadmin enable\fR
.TP
.B test
Run CLI command validation tests.
.SS "System Administration"
.TP
.B system \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
System-level operations and diagnostics: info, check, audit.
.TP
.B preflight \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Pre-installation system checks and compatibility validation.
Verifies OS, kernel, nftables version, and dependency requirements.
.TP
.B polkit \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Polkit authorization validation and group management: check, install, status.
Manages the nftban-admin group for non-root firewall management.
.TP
.B rollback \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Restore previous NFTBan version from backup.
Lists available backups and allows selection for rollback.
.TP
.B update \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Automated updates from git repository with backup and rollback support.
.RS
.IP \fB\-\-check\fR
Check if updates are available without making changes.
.IP \fB\-\-force\fR
Force reinstall even if already at current version.
.IP \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview what would happen without executing changes.
.IP \fB\-\-rollback\fR
Revert to the previous backup.
.IP \fB\-\-list\fR
List available backups.
.RE
.IP
Creates automatic backup before updating. Configurable via /etc/nftban/update.conf.
.TP
.B support \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Collect diagnostic information for troubleshooting. Creates a support bundle tarball.
.RS
.IP \fB\-\-quick\fR
Quick terminal diagnostics without creating a file.
.IP \fB\-\-network\fR
Include network information (ip addr, routes, listening ports).
.IP "\fB\-\-output\fR \fIDIR\fR"
Output directory (default: /tmp).
.RE
.IP
Output: /tmp/nftban-support-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.tar.gz
.br
Collects: version, OS info, nftables ruleset, configs (secrets redacted),
logs (last 24h), health check, service status.
.br
Alias: \fBsupport-bundle\fR
.SS "Debug and Troubleshooting"
.TP
.B debug \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Debug and troubleshooting tools. Subcommands:
.RS
.IP \fBstatus\fR
Show debug status (trace enabled, log level, orphan count).
.IP "\fBenable\fR [\fItype\fR]"
Enable debug trace or verbose logging. Types: trace (default), verbose, all.
.IP "\fBdisable\fR [\fItype\fR]"
Disable debug trace or verbose logging.
.IP "\fBtrace recent\fR [\fIN\fR]"
Show last N trace entries (default: 30).
.IP "\fBtrace orphans\fR [\fIMIN\fR]"
Find stuck scripts (START without END, older than MIN minutes).
.IP \fBtrace stats\fR
Show trace statistics.
.IP "\fBtrace clear\fR [\fIDAYS\fR]"
Rotate trace log, keep DAYS (default: 7).
.IP "\fBlogs\fR [\fITYPE\fR] [\fIN\fR]"
View log files: main, trace, login, bans, all.
.IP "\fBdump\fR [\fIWHAT\fR]"
Dump debug info: config, env, services, nft, all.
.RE
.TP
.B emulate \fIIP\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Simulate packet decision to test firewall rules without actual traffic.
Options: \fB\-\-proto\fR (tcp/udp), \fB\-\-port\fR, \fB\-\-direction\fR (in/out), \fB\-\-json\fR.
Useful for testing before deploying rules.
.TP
.B smoke \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Smoke test suite for CLI health checks. Subcommands:
.RS
.IP \fBrun\fR
Run full smoke test suite (tests all major commands).
.IP \fBquick\fR
Run quick test (core commands only).
.IP "\fBcheck\fR [\fIMIN\fR]"
Check for orphaned traces (stuck scripts).
.IP \fBstats\fR
Show trace statistics.
.RE
.SS "User Interface"
.TP
.B menu
Interactive text-based menu interface.
.TP
.B gui \fR[\fIsubcommand\fR]
Web GUI management: enable, disable, status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format (supported by status, list, services, and other commands).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress banner and non-essential output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show detailed output.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help for specific command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/nftban/nftban.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/nftban/update.conf
Update command configuration (git repo, branch, backup count).
.TP
.I /etc/nftban/conf.d/
Module configuration directory.
.TP
.I /etc/nftban/blacklist.d/
Custom blacklist files.
.TP
.I /etc/nftban/whitelist.d/
Custom whitelist files.
.TP
.I /var/lib/nftban/
Runtime data directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/nftban/geoip/
GeoIP database files.
.TP
.I /var/log/nftban/
Log files directory.
.TP
.I /var/log/nftban/debug_trace.log
Debug trace log (when NFTBAN_DEBUG_TRACE=true).
.TP
.I /var/log/nftban/watchdog.log
Watchdog monitoring log.
.TP
.I /var/lib/nftban/metrics/watchdog.prom
Watchdog Prometheus metrics (for node_exporter textfile collector).
.TP
.I /var/lib/nftban/reports/watchdog/
Saved watchdog reports directory.
.TP
.I /etc/nftban/conf.d/watchdog.conf
Watchdog configuration (thresholds, intervals).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/nftban/
Library and module directory.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/nftban/data/config-schema.json
JSON schema for configuration validation.
.TP
.I /var/lib/nftban/config/schema-state.json
Saved schema state for upgrade drift detection.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check system status:
.B nftban status
.TP
Ban an IP for 1 hour:
.B nftban ban 192.168.1.100 \-\-timeout 3600 \-\-reason "suspicious activity"
.TP
Permanently ban an IP:
.B nftban ban 192.168.1.100 \-\-permanent
.TP
Show statistics dashboard:
.B nftban stats dashboard
.TP
Stats with time filter:
.B nftban stats \-\-last 7d
.TP
Top 20 banned IPs:
.B nftban stats top ips 20
.TP
Export stats to JSON:
.B nftban stats export \-\-format json \-\-output /tmp/stats.json
.TP
Export stats to CSV:
.B nftban stats export \-\-format csv
.TP
Real-time monitoring:
.B nftban stats monitor
.TP
Enable DDoS protection:
.B nftban ddos enable
.TP
GeoIP lookup:
.B nftban geoip lookup 8.8.8.8
.TP
Update threat feeds:
.B nftban feeds update
.TP
List available trust feeds:
.B nftban trust list
.TP
Enable Cloudflare and AWS whitelist:
.B nftban trust enable CLOUDFLARE AWS
.TP
Update all enabled trust feeds:
.B nftban trust update
.TP
Block traffic from China and Russia:
.B nftban country disable CN RU
.TP
List country codes:
.B nftban country list
.TP
JSON status output:
.B nftban status \-\-json
.TP
Enable debug trace:
.B nftban debug enable
.TP
Find stuck scripts:
.B nftban debug trace orphans
.TP
Run smoke test:
.B nftban smoke run
.TP
Quick CLI health check:
.B nftban smoke quick
.TP
View last 50 trace entries:
.B nftban debug trace recent 50
.TP
Full debug dump:
.B nftban debug dump all
.TP
Check system resource health:
.B nftban watchdog status
.TP
Generate watchdog report:
.B nftban watchdog report
.TP
Enable watchdog timer (90-second interval):
.B nftban watchdog enable
.TP
Validate all configuration:
.B nftban configtest
.TP
Verbose configuration validation:
.B nftban config test \-\-verbose
.TP
Audit configuration for drift:
.B nftban configaudit
.TP
Show effective merged config:
.B nftban config show
.TP
Show local overrides vs defaults:
.B nftban config diff
.TP
Check for updates:
.B nftban update \-\-check
.TP
Update to latest version:
.B nftban update
.TP
Force reinstall:
.B nftban update \-\-force
.TP
Rollback to previous version:
.B nftban update \-\-rollback
.TP
Generate support bundle for troubleshooting:
.B nftban support
.TP
Quick terminal diagnostics:
.B nftban support \-\-quick
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
.TP
.B 2
Command not found
.TP
.B 3
Configuration error
